endstreamendobj612 0 obj<</A[1400 0 R 0]/K[1]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj624 0 obj<</E(Musical Performance: Hirari Sato)/K[13]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj625 0 obj<</E(Hirari Sato was introduced with a fuller profile: the first Japanese singer to perform her country's national anthem as a soloist at the Tokyo 2020 Paralympic Games opening ceremony, present in Accra as a goodwill ambassador for the UN Singers Peace Conce\rt, and an artist who has used her music to support communities affected by the Great East Japan Earthquake. She shared her personal commitment to peace advocacy as a citizen of the only nation to have experienced atomic bombing, and her ambition to becom\e the Stevie Wonder of Japan.)/K[14]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj626 0 obj<</A[1405 0 R 0]/K[15]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj627 0 obj<</E(She performed Amazing Grace followed by an original Japanese composition, then a collaborative performance of a traditional Japanese song with students from Hiroo Gakuen.)/K[16]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj622 0 obj<</E(Cultural Performance: Labone Senior High School)/K[11]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj611 0 obj<</A[1399 0 R 0]/K[0]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj623 0 obj<</A[1404 0 R 0]/K[12]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj628 0 obj<</E(Labone Senior High School followed with an energetic performance, drawing a strong response from the floor. The performance built on an existing exchange connection between Labone and Hiroo Gakuen students from an earlier visit to Japan.)/K[17]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj613 0 obj<</E(Cultural Showcase)/K[2]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj614 0 obj<</E(With the evening running later than planned, MCs opened the floor for an informal cultural showcase, originally intended for songs, poems, or dance from delegates' home countries. With the room slower to volunteer than hoped, the MCs adapted in real time \into a casual, good-humoured fashion show format, inviting delegates already dressed in traditional attire to walk forward and share the name, origin, and significance of what they were wearing. The session closed with a full group photograph.)/K[3]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj615 0 obj<</E(Unity Toast and Closing)/K[4]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj617 0 obj<</A[1402 0 R 0]/K[6]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj616 0 obj<</A[1401 0 R 0]/K[5]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj621 0 obj<</E(The evening closed with a Unity Toast dedicated to fruitful, long-term partnerships between Africa and Japan. MCs thanked delegates for a full day that had begun early that morning, and delivered logistics for Day 2: departure by bus from the Mensvic Gran\d Hotel at 8:00 AM sharp, specified as Japan time to avoid ambiguity, a city tour beginning at 1:30 PM, and Drive-branded t-shirts distributed to all participants joining the morning and afternoon activities.)/K[10]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj618 0 obj<</A[1403 0 R 0]/K[7]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj629 0 obj<</A[1406 0 R 0]/K[18]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj619 0 obj<</E(TICAD Youth Drive 2026 ·Report)/K[8]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj620 0 obj<</E(17)/K[9]/P 165 0 R/Pg 26 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj1406 0 obj<</BBox[51.81675 51.60298 543.543 52.35298]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1403 0 obj<</BBox[148.94615 54.561523 452.06036 257.13782]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1401 0 obj<</BBox[47.87554 328.5113 87.640526 331.51242]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1402 0 obj<</BBox[47.87554 445.9948 87.640526 448.99594]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1404 0 obj<</BBox[48.562428 466.10913 271.64716 614.51917]/O/Layo