igure/Type/StructElem>>endobj553 0 obj<</E( )/K[5]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj566 0 obj<</E(Special Remarks: Prof. Mieko Ikegame)/K[18]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H2/T(Special Remarks: Prof. Mieko Ikegame)/Type/StructElem>>endobj567 0 obj<</E(Prof. Mieko Ikegame, introduced light-heartedly as the mother of TICAD, opened by joking that she preferred the title queen of TICAD, since she had not yet received permission from Japan's Ministry of Foreign Affairs for the former.)/K[19]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H3/T(Prof. Mieko Ikegame, introduced light-heartedly as the mother of TICAD, opened by joking that she preferred the title queen of TICAD, since she had not yet received permission from Japan's Ministry of Foreign Affairs for the former.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj568 0 obj<</A[1388 0 R 0]/K[20]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj548 0 obj<</A[1383 0 R 0]/K[0]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj571 0 obj<</E(Culture, dances, music and songs can unite us all. Music is a universal language of the)/K[23]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H3/T(Culture, dances, music and songs can unite us all. Music is a universal language of the)/Type/StructElem>>endobj572 0 obj<</E(humankind.)/K[24]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H3/T(humankind.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj558 0 obj<</E(- Prof. Mieko Ikegame)/K[10]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H4/T(- Prof. Mieko Ikegame)/Type/StructElem>>endobj569 0 obj<</E(She noted that 2026 marks the 70th anniversary of both Japan's and Ghana's United Nations membership, and used the occasion to introduce the United Nations Singers, a group of UN staff members, roughly 65 members from about 45 countries, established just \two years after the UN's founding. She described the group's practice of performing in national costume and in multiple languages as a living symbol of the UN's own principle: unity within diversity.)/K[21]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H3/T(She noted that 2026 marks the 70th anniversary of both Japan's and Ghana's United Nations membership, and used the occasion to introduce the United Nations Singers, a group of UN staff members, roughly 65 members from about 45 countries, established just \two years after the UN's founding. She described the group's practice of performing in national costume and in multiple languages as a living symbol of the UN's own principle: unity within diversity.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj549 0 obj<</A[1384 0 R 0]/K[1]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj573 0 obj<</E(United Nations singers is a symbol of unity with diversity, which is the principle of the United)/K[25]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H3/T(United Nations singers is a symbol of unity with diversity, which is the principle of the United)/Type/StructElem>>endobj574 0 obj<</E(Nations.)/K[26]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H3/T(Nations.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj559 0 obj<</E(- Prof. Mieko Ikegame)/K[11]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H4/T(- Prof. Mieko Ikegame)/Type/StructElem>>endobj570 0 obj<</E(She introduced that evening's performer, Hirari Sato, as a Goodwill Ambassador for the UN Singers Peace Concert, praising the emotional reach of her voice before inviting delegates to enjoy the evening in the spirit it was intended, several delegates had \changed into yukata and kimono for the occasion.)/K[22]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/H3/T(She introduced that evening's performer, Hirari Sato, as a Goodwill Ambassador for the UN Singers Peace Concert, praising the emotional reach of her voice before inviting delegates to enjoy the evening in the spirit it was intended, several delegates had \changed into yukata and kimono for the occasion.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj575 0 obj<</A[1389 0 R 0]/K[27]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj557 0 obj<</E(TICAD Youth Drive 2026 · Report)/K[9]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj560 0 obj<</E(15)/K[12]/P 163 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj1389 0 obj<</BBox[51.81675 51.60298 543.543 52.35298