endstreamendobj424 0 obj<</A[1337 0 R 0]/K[0]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj439 0 obj<</E(The dialogue was structured around two themes. Theme One, Youth Innovation and Economic Opportunity, opened with Hiroshi Yokoyama, who built AXCEL Africa after concluding that Japanese companies visiting Africa rarely left lasting impact without someone d\edicated to building the bridge. )/K[15]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(The dialogue was structured around two themes. Theme One, Youth Innovation and Economic Opportunity, opened with Hiroshi Yokoyama, who built AXCEL Africa after concluding that Japanese companies visiting Africa rarely left lasting impact without someone d\edicated to building the bridge. )/Type/StructElem>>endobj436 0 obj<</A[1340 0 R 0]/K[12]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj438 0 obj<</E(The future of Africa and Japan is not made by big companies, government, and big money alone. It's made by people, one by one, who choose to stand in the empty space and build something together.)/K[14]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(The future of Africa and Japan is not made by big companies, government, and big money alone. It's made by people, one by one, who choose to stand in the empty space and build something together.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj437 0 obj<</E(„ Hiroshi Yokoyama)/K[13]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H3/T(„ Hiroshi Yokoyama)/Type/StructElem>>endobj427 0 obj<</E(Keitai Tsuchihashi continued the theme from the ground level, describing how KAMBANG Farms' drone-spraying business grew from his own frustration sourcing labour in northern Ghana, now delivering 20…30% productivity gains for client farmers.)/K[3]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H4/T(Keitai Tsuchihashi continued the theme from the ground level, describing how KAMBANG Farms' drone-spraying business grew from his own frustration sourcing labour in northern Ghana, now delivering 20…30% productivity gains for client farmers.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj428 0 obj<</A[1338 0 R 0]/K[4]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj431 0 obj<</E(Ghanaians say munica minica, it means I don't have money. But I started this business as a student, with just one plot in an orphanage garden. Even if you don't have money, you can start small. )/K[7]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(Ghanaians say munica minica, it means I don't have money. But I started this business as a student, with just one plot in an orphanage garden. Even if you don't have money, you can start small. )/Type/StructElem>>endobj430 0 obj<</E(-Keitai Tsuchihashi)/K[6]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H1/T(-Keitai Tsuchihashi)/Type/StructElem>>endobj429 0 obj<</E( )/K[5]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj435 0 obj<</E(Theme Two, Bridging Africa…Japan Youth, opened with David Kpondehou, standing in for Prof. Sacko, who shared the origin story of ADNJ itself, born from uniting scattered African associations across Japan, and the nine years of trust-building it took befor\e a Japanese company agreed to a joint venture with him.)/K[11]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(Theme Two, Bridging Africa…Japan Youth, opened with David Kpondehou, standing in for Prof. Sacko, who shared the origin story of ADNJ itself, born from uniting scattered African associations across Japan, and the nine years of trust-building it took befor\e a Japanese company agreed to a joint venture with him.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj432 0 obj<</A[1339 0 R 0]/K[8]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj434 0 obj<</E(This trust for young people is very important, the patience and the capacity to understand, it takes time to realise faith.)/K[10]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(This trust for young people is very important, the patience and the capacity to understand, it takes time to realise faith.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj433 0 obj<</E(-David Kpondehou)/K[9]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H5/T(-David Kpondehou)/Type/StructElem>>endobj443 0 obj<</E(Jewel Hatta closed the panel's individual remarks, describing how moving to Ghana at eighteen reframed her view of the relationship entirely,fromone-directional aidtocomplementaryopportunity. )/K[19]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(Jewel Hatta closed the panel's individual remarks, describing how moving to Ghana at eighteen reframed her view of the relationship entirely,fromone-directional aidtocomplementaryopportunity. )/Type/StructElem>>endobj440 0 obj<</A[1341 0 R 0]/K[16]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj442 0 obj<</E(Ghana opened my eyes in the way that opportunities and problems are complementary.)/K[18]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(Ghana opened my eyes in the way that opportunities and problems are complementary.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj441 0 obj<</E(„ Jewel Hatta)/K[17]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H5/T(„ Jewel Hatta)/Type/StructElem>>endobj444 0 obj<</A[1342 0 R 0]/K[20]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj445 0 obj<</E(The floor opened to audience questions, including from Victor of Chibana International Ghana, who pressed Keitai on whether his drone system could integrate weather prediction, and Haruna Muntala, Executive Director of the I4P Foundation, who asked what h\appens when youth businesses fail.)/K[21]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(The floor opened to audience questions, including from Victor of Chibana International Ghana, who pressed Keitai on whether his drone system could integrate weather prediction, and Haruna Muntala, Executive Director of the I4P Foundation, who asked what h\appens when youth businesses fail.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj446 0 obj<</E(Moderator Terry Otieno closed the session by inviting each panelist for one final message. All four, without coordination, converged on the same theme: take action.)/K[22]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/H2/T(Moderator Terry Otieno closed the session by inviting each panelist for one final message. All four, without coordination, converged on the same theme: take action.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj447 0 obj<</A[1343 0 R 0]/K[23]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj425 0 obj<</E(TICAD Youth Drive 2026 · Report)/K[1]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj426 0 obj<</E(10)/K[2]/P 158 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj1343 0 obj<</BBox[51.81675 51.60298 543.543 52.35298]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1342 0 obj<</BBox[39.161552 101.59779 285.20554 264.3556]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1341 0 obj<</BBox[48.013134 282.46356 50.26398 315.476]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1339 0 obj<</BBox[54.71774 375.26022 58.469154 420.2772]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1338 0 obj<</BBox[54.71774 505.49753 60.328762 605.09314]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1340 0 obj<</BBox[57.25399 685.3524 61.005405 749.8767]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1337 0 obj<</BBox[-5.002135 831.07227 600.476 855.0813]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj18 0 obj<</Annots[]/BleedBox[0.0 7.8299813 595.5 850.07996]/Contents 2944 0 R/CropBox[0.0 7.8299813 595.5 850.07996]/MediaBox[0.0 7.8299813 595.5 850.07996]/Parent 2 0 R/Resources<</ExtGState<</GS0 858 0 R/GS1 859 0 R>>/XObject<</Fm0 71 0 R>>>>/Rotate 0/StructParents 8/Tabs/S/TrimBox[0.0 7.8299813 595.5 850.07996]/Type/Page>>endobj2944 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 237>>stream
