endstreamendobj267 0 obj<</A[1276 0 R 0]/K[1]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj273 0 obj<</E(Third: the relationship between Africa and Japan is being rebuilt person by person, and generation by generation. Not through aid alone, but through nine years of patient trust-building, through drone businesses started with one borrowed acre, through thi\rty-five years of one woman's quiet advocacy finally recognised on a stage in Accra. The future this Drive is building is, quite literally, being built by hand.)/K[7]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj274 0 obj<</E(We are proud to share these Proceedings as a record of what was said, what was decided, and what comes next.)/K[8]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj306 0 obj<</A[1286 0 R 0]/K[40]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj275 0 obj<</E(David Kpondehou, Ami Saito, Terry Otieno, & Yuki Yasumiba Co-chairs, TICAD Youth Drive 2026)/K[9]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj276 0 obj<</E(Organizers Summary)/K[10]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj266 0 obj<</A[1275 0 R 0]/K[0]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj268 0 obj<</E(The TICAD Youth Drive 2026 was convened by ADNJ and AAYN, in partnership with the Government of Ghana, from 13 to 14 August 2026 at the Mensvic Grand Hotel, Accra. It was the fourth in a series of Africa…Japan Youth Drives, and the second to be held on th\e African continent under the banner of a fully realised policy framework, Youth Agenda 2055: The Future We Want.)/K[2]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj269 0 obj<</E(The Drive's two headline outcomes were the official launch of the Africa…Japan Youth Alliance \(AJYA\), a membership-based, youth-owned organization tasked with implementing Youth Agenda 2055's ten action points, and the adoption of the Accra Declaration,\ signed on stage by representatives of the Pan-African Youth Union, AAYN, and ADNJ, carrying the Drive's call to action forward to the African Union, TICAD co-organizers, and global partners including the World Bank, JICA, and UNDP.)/K[3]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj270 0 obj<</E(Day 1 combined high-level policy dialogue with hands-on capacity building, including sessions on digital skills and AI, entrepreneurship, and storytelling for social change, and closed with a Cultural Night celebrating the diversity of both delegations. D\ay 2 shifted to an Innovation and Industry Tour, with workshops hosted by Toyota Tsusho Ghana, AnimaxFyb Studios, and Medulla Digital, followed by a city and cultural tour of Accra.)/K[4]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj277 0 obj<</E(TICAD Youth Drive 2026 in Numbers)/K[11]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj292 0 obj<</A[1285 0 R 0]/K[26]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj278 0 obj<</A[1277 0 R 0]/K[12]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj286 0 obj<</E(285)/K[20]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj293 0 obj<</E(In person youth delegates)/K[27]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj279 0 obj<</A[1278 0 R 0]/K[13]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj300 0 obj<</E(2)/K[34]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj294 0 obj<</E(Countries hosting the )/K[28]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj295 0 obj<</E(Drive series )/K[29]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj296 0 obj<</E(\(Japan & Ghana\))/K[30]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj280 0 obj<</A[1279 0 R 0]/K[14]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj287 0 obj<</E(732)/K[21]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj297 0 obj<</E(People joined the live stream)/K[31]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj282 0 obj<</A[1281 0 R 0]/K[16]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj288 0 obj<</E(4th)/K[22]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj298 0 obj<</E(TICAD Youth)/K[32]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj299 0 obj<</E(Drive)/K[33]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj281 0 obj<</A[1280 0 R 0]/K[15]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj301 0 obj<</E(6)/K[35]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj291 0 obj<</E(Mainstream media outreach: 4 news articles, 1 TV interview, & 1 radio interview)/K[25]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj283 0 obj<</A[1282 0 R 0]/K[17]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj303 0 obj<</E(23)/K[37]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj302 0 obj<</E(Nationalities)/K[36]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj284 0 obj<</A[1283 0 R 0]/K[18]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj289 0 obj<</E(18+)/K[23]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj290 0 obj<</E(Speakers & moderators)/K[24]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj285 0 obj<</A[1284 0 R 0]/K[19]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj305 0 obj<</E(2)/K[39]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj304 0 obj<</E(High schools in cultural exchange: Hiroo Gakuen & Labone Senior)/K[38]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj307 0 obj<</A[1287 0 R 0]/K[41]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj271 0 obj<</E(TICAD Youth Drive 2026 · Report)/K[5]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj272 0 obj<</E(04)/K[6]/P 152 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj1287 0 obj<</BBox[51.81675 51.60298 543.543 52.35298]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1284 0 obj<</BBox[428.73932 89.651 553.28625 211.19681]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1283 0 obj<</BBox[428.73932 212.80615 553.28625 334.35196]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1282 0 obj<</BBox[302.86212 89.651 427.40906 211.19681]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1280 0 obj<</BBox[176.98494 89.651 301.53186 211.19681]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1281 