8 0 R/Prev 2857 0 R/Title(City and Cultural Tour)>>endobj2836 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/First 2855 0 R/Last 2855 0 R/Next 2818 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2854 0 R/Title(Dinner)>>endobj2855 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2836 0 R/Title(Delegates were served dinner using a coupon system, with seating temporarily moved outside to collect food before returning tothe main hall.)>>endobj2854 0 obj<</Count -8/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/First 2871 0 R/Last 2872 0 R/Next 2836 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2870 0 R/Title(Special Recognition: The Bridge Builders Award)>>endobj2871 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Next 2886 0 R/Parent 2854 0 R/Title(Following the performance, Ambassador Dr. Erica Bennett, founder and head of mission of DAFF, with over 45 years of experience in diaspora engagement and pan-African cooperation, addressed the room.)>>endobj2872 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/First 2888 0 R/Last 2888 0 R/Parent 2854 0 R/Prev 2887 0 R/Title(Bring the justicetoAfrica, that's my campaign.)>>endobj2870 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/First 2884 0 R/Last 2885 0 R/Next 2854 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2883 0 R/Title(Performance: Diaspora African Forum- Kids in Tourism)>>endobj2884 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Next 2885 0 R/Parent 2870 0 R/Title(The evening continued with a performance from Kids in Tourism, a youth initiative of the Diaspora African Forum \(DAFF\), an African Union-endorsed nonprofit mission advocating for Africans in the diaspora. The performers were introduced as the grandchild\ren of DAFF's founder, Her Excellency Ambassador Dr. Erica Bennett.)>>endobj2885 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2870 0 R/Prev 2884 0 R/Title(A young performer, introduced as a former Junior Tourism Ambassador, recited an original poem titled Mother Ghana, personifying the nation and touring its regions, natural resources, festivals, cuisine, and heritage sites, referencing landmarks includin\g Cape Coast Castle, Kakum National Park, and Wli Falls, and paying tribute to President John Dramani Mahama, before the group closed with music and dance.)>>endobj2883 0 obj<</Count -3/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/First 2896 0 R/Last 2897 0 R/Next 2870 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2895 0 R/Title(Day 1 Cultural Night)>>endobj2896 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Next 2904 0 R/Parent 2883 0 R/Title(13 August 2026, 8:00…9:45PM · MCs: Caroline Obeng & Terry Otieno)>>endobj2897 0 obj<</Count -7/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/First 2905 0 R/Last 2906 0 R/Parent 2883 0 R/Prev 2904 0 R/Title(Special Remarks: Prof. Mieko Ikegame)>>endobj2895 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/First 2903 0 R/Last 2903 0 R/Next 2883 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2882 0 R/Title(DRIVE)>>endobj2903 0 obj<</Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2895 0 R/Title(2026)>>endobj2882 0 obj<</Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Next 2895 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2869 0 R/Title(TICAD YOUTH)>>endobj2869 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 2880 0 R/Last 2881 0 R/Next 2882 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2853 0 R/Title(Capacity Building: From Vision to Action)>>endobj2880 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Next 2881 0 R/Parent 2869 0 R/Title(Facilitators: Terry Otieno \(ADNJ\) · Yuki Yasumiba \(AAYN\))>>endobj2881 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 2893 0 R/Last 2894 0 R/Parent 2869 0 R/Prev 2880 0 R/Title(A closing capacity-building session translating the day's discussions into concrete next steps, bridging the policy conversations of the morning with the practical, hands-on learning of the sessions that followed.)>>endobj2853 0 obj<</Count -4/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 2867 0 R/Last 2868 0 R/Next 2869 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2835 0 R/Title(Organization for Change: Discovering Your Story)>>endobj2867 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Next 2877 0 R/Parent 2853 0 R/Title(Moderator: Yuki Yasumiba \(AAYN\))>>endobj2868 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 2879 0 R/Last 2879 0 R/Parent 2853 0 R/Prev 2878 0 R/Title(Facts help you to understand, but stories help people care.)>>endobj2835 0 obj<</Count -4/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 2851 0 R/Last 2852 0 R/Next 2853 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2817 0 R/Title(Capacity Building: Digital Skills, AI & Innovation & Entrepreneurship)>>endobj2851 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Next 2864 0 R/Parent 2835 0 R/Title(Moderators: Jewel Hatta, Marina Noda)>>endobj2852 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 2866 0 R/Last 2866 0 R/Parent 2835 0 R/Prev 2865 0 R/Title(His challenge to the room was to see the disruption as an opening rather than only a threat, to identify where new categories of digital and simulation-based work are emerging, and to position themselves early.)>>endobj2817 0 obj<</Count -4/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/First 2833 0 R/Last 2834 0 R/Next 2835 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2801 0 R/Title(Youth Voices: Stories Behind Our Communities)>>endobj2833 0 obj<</Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Next 2848 0 R/Parent 2817 0 R/Title(Moderator: Prof. Mieko Ikegame)>>endobj2834 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/First 2850 0 R/Last 2850 0 R/Parent 2817 0 R/Prev 2849 0 R/Title(Hiroo Gakuen, whose choir is a consistent national gold medallist in Japan, described how a single university lecture on world peace to 900 student volunteers sparked the trip, with 300 students writing letters afterward and a dedicated study group formin\g ahead of the visit.)>>endobj2801 0 obj<</Count -6/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/First 2815 0 R/Last 2816 0 R/Next 2817 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2786 0 R/Title(Inspire Us: Passing the Baton to the Next Generation of Youth Leaders)>>endobj2815 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2829 0 R/Parent 2801 0 R/Title(Speaker: Professor Fred Awaah \(Board Chairman, National Sports Authority, Ghana\))>>endobj2816 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/First 2831 0 R/Last 2832 0 R/Parent 2801 0 R/Prev 2830 0 R/Title(When you're lost, choose what scares you or what excites you.)>>endobj2786 0 obj<</Count -6/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/First 2799 0 R/Last 2800 0 R/Next 2801 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 2766 0 R/Title(-Keitai Tsuchihashi)>>endobj2799 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Next 2812 0 R/Parent 2786 0 R/Title(Theme Two, Bridging Africa…Japan