 IN PARTNERSHIP WITH)>>endobj2572 0 obj<</Count -3/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/First 2696 0 R/Last 2697 0 R/Next 2360 0 R/Parent 2100 0 R/Prev 2695 0 R/Title(Outcomes of the Drive)>>endobj2696 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2722 0 R/Parent 2572 0 R/Title(The Africa…Japan Youth Alliance \(AJYA\))>>endobj2697 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2572 0 R/Prev 2722 0 R/Title(Media Coverage & News Reports)>>endobj2695 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/First 2720 0 R/Last 2721 0 R/Next 2572 0 R/Parent 2100 0 R/Prev 2694 0 R/Title(Day 2 Programme - 14 August 2026: Innovation & Industry Tour)>>endobj2720 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2721 0 R/Parent 2695 0 R/Title(Innovation Workshop: Youth at the Centre of Industrial Innovation)>>endobj2721 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2695 0 R/Prev 2720 0 R/Title(City and Cultural Tour)>>endobj2694 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/First 2719 0 R/Last 2719 0 R/Next 2695 0 R/Parent 2100 0 R/Prev 2571 0 R/Title(Day 1 - Cultural Night)>>endobj2719 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2694 0 R/Title(Evening Programme)>>endobj2571 0 obj<</Count -10/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/First 2692 0 R/Last 2693 0 R/Next 2694 0 R/Parent 2100 0 R/Prev 2359 0 R/Title(Day 1 Programme - 13 August 2026)>>endobj2692 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2717 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Title(Arrival, Registration & the Africa…JapanVillage)>>endobj2693 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2718 0 R/Title(Reflections, Key Takeaways & Adoption of the Accra Declaration)>>endobj2718 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2693 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2741 0 R/Title(Capacity Building: From Vision to Action)>>endobj2741 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2718 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2757 0 R/Title(Capacity Building: Digital Skills, AI & Innovation & Entrepreneurship Organization for Change: Discovering Your Story)>>endobj2757 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2741 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2775 0 R/Title(Inspire Us: Passing the Baton to the Next Generation of Youth Leaders Youth Voices: Stories Behind Our Communities)>>endobj2775 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2757 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2774 0 R/Title(High-Level Keynote Dialogue)>>endobj2774 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2775 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2756 0 R/Title(Musical Performance)>>endobj2756 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2774 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2740 0 R/Title(Official Launch of the Africa…Japan Youth Alliance \(AJYA\))>>endobj2740 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2756 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2717 0 R/Title(Keynote Address: TICAD & Youth Action)>>endobj2717 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2740 0 R/Parent 2571 0 R/Prev 2692 0 R/Title(Welcome Remarks)>>endobj2722 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2697 0 R/Parent 2572 0 R/Prev 2696 0 R/Title(The Accra Declaration)>>endobj2569 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2690 0 R/Parent 2359 0 R/Title(Acknowledgements)>>endobj2570 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2359 0 R/Prev 2691 0 R/Title(Drive Format)>>endobj2691 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2570 0 R/Parent 2359 0 R/Prev 2716 0 R/Title(TICAD Youth Drive 2026 in Numbers)>>endobj2716 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2691 0 R/Parent 2359 0 R/Prev 2690 0 R/Title(Organizers Summary)>>endobj2690 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Next 2716 0 R/Parent 2359 0 R/Prev 2569 0 R/Title(Foreword)>>endobj2698 0 obj<</Count -4/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/First 2723 0 R/Last 2724 0 R/Next 2725 0 R/Parent 2574 0 R/Title(Acknowledgements)>>endobj2699 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/First 2726 0 R/Last 2727 0 R/Parent 2574 0 R/Prev 2725 0 R/Title(Drive Format)>>endobj2726 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2727 0 R/Parent 2699 0 R/Title(The TICAD Youth Drive 2026 combined a high-level plenary format, welcome remarks, keynote addresses, and a moderated keynote dialogue, with hands-on, interactive capacity-building sessions, storytelling exercises, digital skills training, and small-group \facilitation. Day 2 extended the format further into applied, on-site learning through industry visits and a cultural tour, reflecting the Drive's core philosophy: policy dialogue alone does not build capacity, direct exposure does.)>>endobj2727 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/First 2746 0 R/Last 2746 0 R/Parent 2699 0 R/Prev 2726 0 R/Title(Policy dialogue alone does not build capacity, direct exposure does.)>>endobj2725 0 obj<</Count -4/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/First 2744 0 R/Last 2745 0 R/Next 2699 0 R/Parent 2574 0 R/Prev 2698 0 R/Title(Foreword)>>endobj2744 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2758 0 R/Parent 2725 0 R/Title(The fourth TICAD Youth Drive brought together an extraordinary, committed community of young Africans and Japanese, gathered in Accra under a single theme: Youth Agenda 2055, From Vision to Action.)>>endobj2745 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2725 0 R/Prev 2759 0 R/Title(Second: this generation is not waiting for permission. Across nearly every session, from the keynote dialogue to the capacity-building floor, the same message surfaced independently, again and again: take action, start small, don't wait for institutions. \That convergence, unprompted and unrehearsed, is itself a form of evidence.)>>endobj2759 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2745 0 R/Parent 2725 0 R/Prev 2758 0 R/Title(First: the vision has become policy, and the policy has become an institution. What began as young people simply being asked what future they wanted has, over eighteen months, become Youth Agenda 2055: The Future We Want, launched at TICAD9 in Yokohama. I\n Accra, that policy took its next form: the Africa…Japan Youth Alliance, a standing, youth-owned structure with a Council, a Secretariat, and an Advisory Panel already in motion.)>>endobj2758 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2759 0 R/Parent 2725 0 R/Prev 2744 0 R/Title(Of everything shared across these two days, three points stand out.)>>endobj2746 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2727 0 R/Title(- The Drive's core philosophy)>>endobj2723 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2742 0 R/Parent 2698 0 R/Title(The African Diaspora Network Japan \(ADNJ\) and the Africa Asia Youth Nest \(AAYN\) extend their sincere gratitude to the Government of Ghana, and in particular the Ministry of Youth Development and Empowerment, for generously hosting the TICAD Youth Driv\e 2026, and for its steadfast political support in placing the Drive on Ghana's official Youth Month calendar of events.)>>endobj2724 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2698 0 R/Prev 2743 0 R/Title(We are grateful to Terry Otieno, Policy and Programmes Lead, Africa Diaspora Network Japan \(ADNJ\), for compiling and editing this report.)>>endobj2743 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2724 0 R/Parent 2698 0 R/Prev 2742 0 R/Title(We are especially grateful to the Pan-African Youth Union, the AfCFTA Policy Network, UNECA, the Embassy of Japan in Ghana, the National Youth Authority of Ghana, and the Diaspora African Forum, for their partnership and presence throughout the Drive. Fin\ally, we thank the young delegates themselves, from Ghana, from across the African continent, and from Japan, whose energy, honesty, and willingness to take the stage made this Drive what it was.)>>endobj2742 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2743 0 R/Parent 2698 0 R/Prev 2723 0 R/Title(We gratefully acknowledge the contributions of our core partners and sponsors, including JICA, UNDP, Toyota Tsusho, SMBC, Shibusawa & Company, AnimaxFyb Studios, Creative Studio Academy, and the many other organizations whose support made this Drive possi\ble.)>>endobj2762 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/First 2777 0 R/Last 2778 0 R/Next 2763 0 R/Parent 2748 0 R/Title(Hon. George Opare Addo, Ghana's Minister of Youth Development and Empowerment, officially declared the Drive open, setting a tone of partnership over dependency.)>>endobj2763 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/First 2779 0 R/Last 2780 0 R/Parent 2748 0 R/Prev 2762 0 R/Title(Dr. Zuzana Schwidrowski, Director of UNECA's Socio-Economic Development Division, could not attend in person; her remarks were delivered on her behalf by Mrs. Caroline Obeng.)>>endobj2761 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/First 2776 0 R/Last 2776 0 R/Next 2748 0 R/Parent 2729 0 R/Prev 2747 0 R/Title(Arrival, Registration & the Africa- Japan Village)>>endobj2776 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/First 2795 0 R/Last 2795 0 R/Parent 2761 0 R/Title(The Drive opened with participant check-in alongside the Africa…Japan Village exhibition space, an informal networking area bringing together African and Japanese youth, policymakers, development partners, and the private sector, accompanied by a cultural\ performance.)>>endobj2795 0 obj<</Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2776 0 R/Title(8:50 … 9:50 AM)>>endobj2779 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2780 0 R/Parent 2763 0 R/Title(Young people should not simply be discussed as the future. You are partners in shaping the present)>>endobj2780 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2763 0 R/Prev 2779 0 R/Title(9:50 … 10:05 AM)>>endobj2777 0 obj<</Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Next 2778 0 R/Parent 2762 0 R/Title(Africa does not need Japan's charity. And Japan does not need Africa merely as a market or a source of labor. What we need is partnership.Ž)>>endobj2778 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/First 2796 0 R/Last 2796 0 R/Parent 2762 0 R/Prev 2777 0 R/Title(-Hon. George Opare Addo)>>endobj2796 0 obj<</Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2778 0 R/Title(TICAD Youth Drive 2026 · Report)>>endobj2760 0 obj<</Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2747 0 R/Title(8:00 … 8:50 AM)>>endobj2783 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2765 0 R/Title(10:05 … 10:20 AM)>>endobj2782 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2765 0 R/Parent 2749 0 R/Prev 2781 0 R/Title(You may think I look Japanese, but I'm a UN person. And if you ask where your heart is, I say my heart is for Africa.)>>endobj2781 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2782 0 R/Parent 2749 0 R/Prev 2764 0 R/Title(Prof. Mieko Ikegame, who spent 33 years at the United Nations and worked across 30 African countries, took the room through TICAD's real origin story: born out of the UN system rather than a bilateral agreement, and built specifically to ensure Africa's o\wn voice led the process.)>>endobj2798 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/First 2811 0 R/Last 2811 0 R/Next 2785 0 R/Parent 2766 0 R/Prev 2810 0 R/Title(The future of Africa and Japan is not made by big companies, government, and big money alone. It's made by people, one by one, who choose to stand in the empty space and build something together.)>>endobj2811 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/First 2825 0 R/Last 2825 0 R/Parent 2798 0 R/Title(„ Hiroshi Yokoyama)>>endobj2810 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Next 2798 0 R/Parent 2766 0 R/Prev 2797 0 R/Title(The dialogue was structured around two themes. Theme One, Youth Innovation and Economic Opportunity, opened with Hiroshi Yokoyama, who built AXCEL Africa after concluding that Japanese companies visiting Africa rarely left lasting impact without someone d\edicated to building the bridge.)>>endobj2797 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/First 2809 0 R/Last 2809 0 R/Next 2810 0 R/Parent 2766 0 R/Prev 2784 0 R/Title(Terry Otieno and Ami Saito officially launched the Africa…Japan Youth Alliance, the standing structure called for within Youth Agenda 2055. Terry outlined AJYA's operating structure: a Council meeting quarterly, a five-team Secretariat \(conferences, outr\each, policy support, community management, and fundraising\) meeting biweekly, and an Advisory Panel with JICA and UNDP meeting monthly.)>>endobj2809 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2797 0 R/Title(TICAD Youth Drive 2026 · Report)>>endobj2825 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2811 0 R/Title(Keitai Tsuchihashi continued the theme from the ground level, describing how KAMBANG Farms' drone-spraying business grew from his own frustration sourcing labour in northern Ghana, now delivering 20…30% productivity gains for client farmers.)>>endobj2814 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2800 0 R/Title(11:35 AM … 12:30 PM)>>endobj2813 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Next 2800 0 R/Parent 2786 0 R/Prev 2828 0 R/Title(The floor opened to audience questions, including from Victor of Chibana International Ghana, who pressed Keitai on whether his drone system could integrate weather prediction, and Haruna Muntala, Executive Director of the I4P Foundation, who asked what h\appens when youth businesses fail.)>>endobj2828 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/First 2845 0 R/Last 2845 0 R/Next 2813 0 R/Parent 2786 0 R/Prev 2827 0 R/Title(Ghana opened my eyes in the way that opportunities and problems are complementary.)>>endobj2845 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2828 0 R/Title(„ Jewel Hatta)>>endobj2827 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Next 2828 0 R/Parent 2786 0 R/Prev 2812 0 R/Title(Jewel Hatta closed the panel's individual remarks, describing how moving to Ghana at eighteen reframed her view of the relationship entirely,fromone-directional aidtocomplementaryopportunity.)>>endobj2812 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/First 2826 0 R/Last 2826 0 R/Next 2827 0 R/Parent 2786 0 R/Prev 2799 0 R/Title(This trust for young people is very important, the patience and the capacity to understand, it takes time to realise faith.)>>endobj2826 0 obj<</Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2812 0 R/Title(-David Kpondehou)>>endobj2831 0 obj<</Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Next 2832 0 R/Parent 2816 0 R/Title(- Kotone Sakamoto)>>endobj2832 0 obj<</Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2816 0 R/Prev 2831 0 R/Title(1:30 … 2:40 PM)>>endobj2830 0 obj<</Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Next 2816 0 R/Parent 2801 0 R/Prev 2847 0 R/Title(Kotone Sakamoto, a 22-year-old Japanese student, shared how a solo, budget trip to Africa two years ago grew into travel across 18 African countries, including hitchhiking from Senegal to Morocco, now living in Benin while teaching Japanese and running a \46,000-follower Instagram account sharing real Africa with a Japanese audience.)>>endobj2847 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/First 2862 0 R/Last 2863 0 R/Next 2830 0 R/Parent 2801 0 R/Prev 2846 0 R/Title(If Fred did it, we can also do it.)>>endobj2862 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2863 0 R/Parent 2847 0 R/Title(- Prof. Fred Awaah)>>endobj2863 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/First 2876 0 R/Last 2876 0 R/Parent 2847 0 R/Prev 2862 0 R/Title(Segment: Small or Any Beginnings)>>endobj2846 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/First 2861 0 R/Last 2861 0 R/Next 2847 0 R/Parent 2801 0 R/Prev 2829 0 R/Title(Failure is an integral part of the success story.)>>endobj2861 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2846 0 R/Title(- Prof. Fred Awaah)>>endobj2829 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2846 0 R/Parent 2801 0 R/Prev 2815 0 R/Title(Professor Fred Awaah shared a career built on repeated setbacks that ultimately compounded into success, from losing his first bid to lead Ghana's students, to losing a Student Loan Trust Fund board seat to a technicality despite winning 76% of the vote, \to eventually becoming Secretary-General of the All Africa Students Union. He completed two PhDs, one in Public Administration through the University of Burundi and one in ICT Education through a World Bank scholarship, both largely during COVID-era lockd\owns.)>>endobj2876 0 obj<</Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2863 0 R/Title(Speaker: Kotone Sakamoto \(Student, Keio University\))>>endobj2850 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2834 0 R/Title(2:40 … 3:20 PM)>>endobj2849 0 obj<</Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Next 2834 0 R/Parent 2817 0 R/Prev 2848 0 R/Title(An interactive storytelling and dialogue session connecting Ghanaian and Japanese students. Labone Senior High School, founded in 1949 and expanded after independence in 1957 under Dr. Kwame Nkrumah, shared its 75-year history and motto, Primus Semper Au\rora. Students described wanting to be the voice, the legacy, and the bridge of the exchange.)>>endobj2848 0 obj<</Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Next 2849 0 R/Parent 2817 0 R/Prev 2833 0 R/Title(Participating Schools: Hiroo Gakuen School of Music \(Tokyo\) · Labone Senior High School \(Ghana\))>>endobj2866 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2852 0 R/Title(3:25 … 3:55 PM)>>endobj2865 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Next 2852 0 R/Parent 2835 0 R/Prev 2864 0 R/Title(Ray Fiifi introduced Medulla Digital's role as a channel partner for Unity Technologies, whose real-time 3D platform powers a majority of top mobile games and virtual and augmented reality applications. He walked the room through Unity's use in simulation\-based training, from excavator operation to smart agriculture, and framed the session around a central tension: Africa's coming youth dividend, set against an AI-driven wave of job automation.)>>endobj2864 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Next 2865 0 R/Parent 2835 0 R/Prev 2851 0 R/Title(Speakers: Ray Fiifi \(Chief Learning Officer, Medulla Digital Academy\))>>endobj2879 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 2892 0 R/Last 2892 0 R/Parent 2868 0 R/Title(- Yuki Yasumiba)>>endobj2878 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Next 2868 0 R/Parent 2853 0 R/Prev 2877 0 R/Title(Yuki Yasumiba, Co-founder of AAYN, led an interactive storytelling exercise, organizing delegates into small, deliberately mixed-nationality groups to practise sharing their personal stories. Her framing centred on the difference between facts and narrati\ve in driving social change.)>>endobj2877 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Next 2878 0 R/Parent 2853 0 R/Prev 2867 0 R/Title(Speaker: Marina Noda \(International Development Specialist, Umikaji Link\))>>endobj2892 0 obj<</Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2879 0 R/Title(4:25 … 4:45 PM)>>endobj2893 0 obj<</Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Next 2894 0 R/Parent 2881 0 R/Title(4:50 … 5:20 PM)>>endobj2894 0 obj<</Count -4/Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/First 2901 0 R/Last 2902 0 R/Parent 2881 0 R/Prev 2893 0 R/Title(Reflections, Key Takeaways & Adoption of the Accra Declaration)>>endobj2901 0 obj<</Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Next 2909 0 R/Parent 2894 0 R/Title(Terry Otieno and Yuki Yasumiba guided delegates through a reflections segment before moving to the signing of the Accra Declaration. Yuki read the opening paragraphs of the preamble to the room before the signing ceremony began.)>>endobj2902 0 obj<</Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2894 0 R/Prev 2910 0 R/Title(The Drive closed the formal programme with a group photo session, a media corner for press interviews, and open networking among delegates.)>>endobj2910 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/First 2916 0 R/Last 2916 0 R/Next 2902 0 R/Parent 2894 0 R/Prev 2909 0 R/Title(If we are moving together we can arrive. This is the Africa that you want. We have to build it together.)>>endobj2916 0 obj<</Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2910 0 R/Title(- President Moumouni Dialla, at the signing of the Accra Declaration)>>endobj2909 0 obj<</Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Next 2910 0 R/Parent 2894 0 R/Prev 2901 0 R/Title(President Moumouni Dialla of the Pan-African Youth Union and Ami Saito, Co-founder of AAYN, signed the Declaration on stage on behalf of their respective organizations, with copies also signed by ADNJ representatives.)>>endobj2905 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Next 2913 0 R/Parent 2897 0 R/Title(Prof. Mieko Ikegame, introduced light-heartedly as the mother of TICAD, opened by joking that she preferred the title queen of TICAD, since she had not yet received permission from Japan's Ministry of Foreign Affairs for the former.)>>endobj2906 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2897 0 R/Prev 2914 0 R/Title(She introduced that evening's performer, Hirari Sato, as a Goodwill Ambassador for the UN Singers Peace Concert, praising the emotional reach of her voice before inviting delegates to enjoy the evening in the spirit it was intended, several delegates had \changed into yukata and kimono for the occasion.)>>endobj2904 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/First 2911 0 R/Last 2912 0 R/Next 2897 0 R/Parent 2883 0 R/Prev 2896 0 R/Title(Evening Programme)>>endobj2911 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Next 2912 0 R/Parent 2904 0 R/Title(After a long first day of policy dialogue and capacity building, delegates gathered for an evening of music, food, and open cultural exchange. MCs Caroline and Terry kept the programme intentionally brisk, mindful that participants had been on their feet \since early morning.)>>endobj2912 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2904 0 R/Prev 2911 0 R/Title(The evening opened with a performance from the Sanka cultural troupe, followed by brief opening remarks declaring the Cultural Night officially open on behalf of the TICAD Youth Drive 2026 committee.)>>endobj2914 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/First 2919 0 R/Last 2919 0 R/Next 2906 0 R/Parent 2897 0 R/Prev 2918 0 R/Title(Nations.)>>endobj2919 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2914 0 R/Title(- Prof. Mieko Ikegame)>>endobj2918 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Next 2914 0 R/Parent 2897 0 R/Prev 2921 0 R/Title(United Nations singers is a symbol of unity with diversity, which is the principle of the United)>>endobj2921 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Next 2918 0 R/Parent 2897 0 R/Prev 2917 0 R/Title(She noted that 2026 marks the 70th anniversary of both Japan's and Ghana's United Nations membership, and used the occasion to introduce the United Nations Singers, a group of UN staff members, roughly 65 members from about 45 countries, established just \two years after the UN's founding. She described the group's practice of performing in national costume and in multiple languages as a living symbol of the UN's own principle: unity within diversity.)>>endobj2917 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/First 2920 0 R/Last 2920 0 R/Next 2921 0 R/Parent 2897 0 R/Prev 2913 0 R/Title(humankind.)>>endobj2920 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2917 0 R/Title(- Prof. Mieko Ikegame)>>endobj2913 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Next 2917 0 R/Parent 2897 0 R/Prev 2905 0 R/Title(Culture, dances, music and songs can unite us all. Music is a universal language of the)>>endobj2888 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2872 0 R/Title(- Prof. Mieko Ikegame)>>endobj2887 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Next 2872 0 R/Parent 2854 0 R/Prev 2900 0 R/Title(Thank you foreverybodywhosupportedmeandhelpedme to carry the mission for Africa.)>>endobj2900 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Next 2887 0 R/Parent 2854 0 R/Prev 2908 0 R/Title(Visibly moved, Prof. Ikegame accepted the award with brief remarks.)>>endobj2908 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/First 2915 0 R/Last 2915 0 R/Next 2900 0 R/Parent 2854 0 R/Prev 2907 0 R/Title(NEPAD. Shehas servedthiscontinent.)>>endobj2915 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2908 0 R/Title(-Amb. Dr. Erica Bennett, presenting the award)>>endobj2907 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Next 2908 0 R/Parent 2854 0 R/Prev 2899 0 R/Title(Shehas worked tirelesslyforAfricathroughtheAfricanUnion,throughtheUN,through)>>endobj2899 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Next 2907 0 R/Parent 2854 0 R/Prev 2886 0 R/Title(Ambassador Bennett then surprised Prof. Mieko Ikegame with DAFF's Bridge Builders Award, previously presented to heads of state and to Winnie Mandela, recognising 35 years of Prof. Ikegame's work for Africa across the African Union, the United Nations, an\d NEPAD.)>>endobj2886 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/First 2898 0 R/Last 2898 0 R/Next 2899 0 R/Parent 2854 0 R/Prev 2871 0 R/Title(This kind of bridge, linking the youth from Japan and the youth from Ghana, is exactly what the heads of state want to see.)>>endobj2898 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2886 0 R/Title(- Amb. Dr. Erica Bennett)>>endobj2858 0 obj<</Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2838 0 R/Title(After the individual lunch session, delegates joined a guided tour of Accra's culture and history, visiting the Kwame Nkrumah Memorial Park, the National Museum of Ghana, the Accra Arts Centre, and Black Star Square, closing the Drive with a direct experi\ence of the city that hosted it.)>>endobj2857 0 obj<</Count -4/Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/First 2874 0 R/Last 2875 0 R/Next 2838 0 R/Parent 2818 0 R/Prev 2856 0 R/Title(Innovation Workshop: Youth at the Centre of Industrial Innovation)>>endobj2874 0 obj<</Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Next 2889 0 R/Parent 2857 0 R/Title(Delegates split across three parallel innovation sessions hosted by Drive sponsors:)>>endobj2875 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/First 2891 0 R/Last 2891 0 R/Parent 2857 0 R/Prev 2890 0 R/Title(Medulla Digital Office)>>endobj2856 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/First 2873 0 R/Last 2873 0 R/Next 2857 0 R/Parent 2818 0 R/Prev 2837 0 R/Title(Innovation & Industry Tour)>>endobj2873 0 obj<</Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2856 0 R/Title(8:30 AM … 12:00 PM)>>endobj2891 0 obj<</Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2875 0 R/Title(1:00 … 5:00 PM · 100 participants)>>endobj2890 0 obj<</Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Next 2875 0 R/Parent 2857 0 R/Prev 2889 0 R/Title(AnimaxFyb Studios)>>endobj2889 0 obj<</Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Next 2890 0 R/Parent 2857 0 R/Prev 2874 0 R/Title(Toyota Tsusho Ghana)>>endobj2820 0 obj<</Count -2/Dest[29 0 R/Fit]/First 2839 0 R/Last 2840 0 R/Parent 2803 0 R/Title(The Africa…Japan Youth Alliance \(AJYA\))>>endobj2839 0 obj<</Dest[29 0 R/Fit]/Next 2840 0 R/Parent 2820 0 R/Title(The Africa…Japan Youth Alliance is a new, youth-owned, youth-run organization, formally launched at the TICAD Youth Drive 2026. It is membership-based, open to individuals and organizations from anywhere in the world who share its vision.)>>endobj2840 0 obj<</Dest[29 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2820 0 R/Prev 2839 0 R/Title(AJYA's mandate is to carry forward the ten action points of Youth Agenda 2055, spanning inclusive education, youth health and wellbeing, economic empowerment and entrepreneurship, peace, security and youth participation in decision-making, youth mobility \and exchange, social cohesion, and climate resilience and sustainability.)>>endobj2769 0 obj<</Count -9/Dest[32 0 R/Fit]/First 2789 0 R/Last 2790 0 R/Parent 2751 0 R/Title(Mainstream Media Coverage)>>endobj2789 0 obj<</Dest[32 0 R/Fit]/Next 2804 0 R/Parent 2769 0 R/Title(1.     Livestream TICAD Youth Drive 2026 Ghana: https://www.youtube.com/live/h0JCTr1-yug?si=OisJwyZXyJCmdJUi)>>endobj2790 0 obj<</Dest[32 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2769 0 R/